<section class="rd-help">
  <h2>Quick setup</h2><ol><li>Enable <strong>This scene has Rotating Elements</strong> in Scene Configuration.</li><li>Click <strong>Target tile</strong> on the floating window, then click the tile on the scene. The module switches to Tiles mode. Escape cancels.</li><li>The tile ID appears and a matching mask is applied automatically. A newly assigned tile stays paused.</li><li>Use <strong>Start / Pause / Reverse</strong> on the floating window.</li></ol>
  <h2>Matching masks</h2><p>Keep the mask image beside the tile image with the same filename stem:</p><p><code>Dungeon.webp</code><br>→ <code>Dungeon_mask.png</code> or <code>Dungeon_Mask.png</code><br>WebP artwork also checks <code>Dungeon_mask.webp</code> / <code>Dungeon_Mask.webp</code></p><p>Otherwise open Settings and use <strong>Browse / Upload</strong>. The file picker supports existing files and uploads where your account has permission.</p>
  <h2>Save = apply walls</h2><p>In Settings, choose or target a tile, choose its mask, then click <strong>Save & apply masks</strong>. Walls are built automatically. Clear the mask and save to remove its generated walls. Black is solid; white/transparent is open. Match the mask to the unrotated artwork.</p>
  <h2>Automatic riders</h2><p>Journal pins and lights already placed on a floor follow it automatically. No selection lists are needed. Light cones rotate; journal links and light appearance are preserved.</p><p>Floor detection uses tile transparency. For opaque images or overlapping rings, use <strong>Advanced → Floor region → Radial bands</strong>. Example: <code>0.5-1</code> for an outer ring. Off-floor objects stay stationary.</p>
  <h2>Settings vs controls</h2><p>Settings is for setup; rotation controls stay in the floating window. The Settings target button fills the form; save to apply. The floating target shortcut saves immediately.</p><p>A GM must view the scene. Disable Fog Exploration for rotating encounters. This is a Foundry v11 release candidate.</p>
  <p>Complete instructions: <code>modules/rotating-dungeon/docs/HELP.md</code> in the installed module.</p>
<h3>Start appears to do nothing</h3><p>Foundry’s game pause also freezes rotating floors. Press Space to unpause. At 0.5°/second, rotation is only 5° in ten seconds. Engine errors appear in the floating controls; fix the error and use Resume engine.</p><p>Automatic mask matching lists existing files in the tile’s folder. If your host cannot list that folder, use Browse / Upload.</p></section>
